; test_build_check.ml's "forge check"/"forge build"/"forge test" cases shell
; out to a real `march check` subprocess (forge/lib/cmd_build.ml's check_all).
; It was QUARANTINED (2026-07-24) on two problems, both now resolved:
;   1. CI/local divergence — CI (fresh checkout: no `.march-version` pin, no
;      ~/.march/current global, no `march` on PATH) resolved to a bare `march`
;      that did not exist, so every subprocess failed identically ("typecheck
;      failed"); locally the suite silently exercised the installed release via
;      the global symlink, not the build under test. FIXED by making the suite
;      HERMETIC: the rule below passes the just-built compiler as MARCH_TEST_BIN
;      (`%{bin:march}`, which dune also builds) and setup_hermetic_march symlinks
;      it as `march` on a private PATH with an empty MARCH_HOME. Host-independent.
;   2. A real constructor-resolution bug (bare `Bar(_)` pattern on a value of a
;      known type reported ambiguous against stdlib `Plot.Bar`). FIXED in
;      lib/typecheck/typecheck.ml (the ambiguity diagnostic now defers to a
;      unique expected-type resolution).
(executable
 (name test_build_check)
 (modules test_build_check)
 (libraries march_forge alcotest unix qcheck-core qcheck-alcotest march_cas))

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (action
  (setenv MARCH_TEST_BIN %{bin:march}
   (run %{exe:test_build_check.exe}))))

